WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
Hey, welcome to SpaceX Daily, episode two.

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:06.000
It's June 13th, 2026, and I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.300
From Starbase to orbit, here's your SpaceX rundown.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.760
Raptor 3's full-flow staged combustion cycle

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.760
and simplified turbo-mackenery cut the idiot index

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.340
on each engine, moving Starship closer

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.980
to rapid reuse economics.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.000
Raptor 3 achieves higher chamber pressure

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.060
than any prior methalox engine

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.760
through a full-flow staged combustion cycle

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.400
that roots all propellant through both turbo pumps.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:34.440
The redesign eliminates the gas generator and many valves,

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.740
lowering part count and production time.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:40.120
thrust now exceeds 280 TF

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.400
while specific impulse remains competitive

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.440
for both sea level and vacuum variance.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.520
These gains directly address the open question

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.020
of engine production rate versus Starship demand.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.220
SpaceX also opened pre-orders for a full-scale replica

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.520
of the Raptor engine bell aimed at collectors

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.900
in educational displays.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.520
The hardware matches the outer geometry

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.840
of the flight article down to the nozzle contour

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.220
and mounting flange, with production using the same additive

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:08.740
and subtractive processes as flight hardware.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.160
Deliveries are scheduled after the next production block

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.160
clears flight units.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.120
SpaceX is counting down to a Falcon 9 lift-off

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.940
from Vandenberg Space Force Base,

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.920
carrying additional Starlink satellites.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.580
The mission uses the same booster fleet

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.040
that has already demonstrated multiple reflites

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.180
from the California pad.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:30.660
Live coverage will stream on the company's usual channels

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:33.760
with pre-launch commentary beginning roughly 90 minutes

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.700
before lift-off.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:38.860
Viewers can track the expected instantaneous launch window

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:41.020
and first-stage recovery on the drone ship.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:43.760
The flight continues the steady cadence

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.360
from the California site and keeps the Falcon fleet

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.900
on its record reuse pace.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.500
One thing worth watching is Blue Origin's New Glenn prototype

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.740
which suffered a pad explosion during a recent Florida test.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:58.680
The incident removes a near-term competitor

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.200
from the heavy-lift manifest

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.580
and shifts some NASA lunar cargo planning timelines.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.520
It highlights the technical risk still present

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:07.820
in new booster development,

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.880
even after years of investment.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:13.260
SpaceX's own Starship program continues

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:16.200
to face similar unknowns around booster catch hardware

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.240
and rapid turnaround.

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:21.000
A successful New Glenn reflite would be required

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.680
to restore schedule confidence for affected missions.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.360
The IPO Prospectus earmarks a portion

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.520
of the $75 billion raised for low-earth orbit infrastructure,

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.540
artificial intelligence compute

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.340
and additional launcher capacity.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.720
The filing lists Starlink subscriber metrics

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.460
and launch cadence as primary revenue drivers.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:45.620
Proceeds are expected to accelerate both orbital data center

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.780
concepts and next generation Raptor production lines.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.320
On the AI front, SpaceX leased capacity

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.740
in the Colossus 1 facility to enthropic after XAI

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.300
reported elevated inference latency on rock workloads.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.380
The move reallocates a portion of the Memphis supercluster

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.600
while XAI expands its own racks.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:10.320
With enthropic using the GPUs for large model training runs

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.620
that require high bandwidth interconnects.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:15.060
The lease terms remain confidential

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:18.120
but are described as short-term bridge capacity.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:21.160
Aerospace firms report that AI tools

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:24.140
are being deployed to handle repetitive engineering tasks

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:26.820
amid a persistent shortage of qualified technicians

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:27.740
and analysts.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.680
The software assists with wiring harness routing checks

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.740
and anomaly detection and test data

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.620
rather than displacing headcount.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.080
SpaceX has not disclosed its internal usage

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.120
but operates in the same labor market.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:44.180
80 self-taxes residents filed suit claiming

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:46.780
repeated starship static fires and launches

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.160
have caused structural damage to homes

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.060
through vibration and overpressure.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.660
The complaint seeks injunctive relief

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:56.840
and monetary damages tied to specific launch dates.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:01.060
SpaceX has not yet filed a response in the public docket.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.800
Resolution would likely require either negotiated mitigation

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.340
or court ordered limits on test cadence.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.800
The suit names 80 plaintiffs and references vibration measurements

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.800
from multiple test events at the Boca Chica site.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.520
Plaintiffs alleged that overpressure events exceeded levels

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:21.000
previously reviewed in environmental assessments

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:21.920
for the facility.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.180
No trial date has been set

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.820
and the case remains in early procedural stages

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.160
in Texas State Court.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.820
Separate environmental organizations

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:33.600
sued to block a land exchange between SpaceX

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.900
and the US Fish and Wildlife Service near Boca Chica.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.140
The swap would give SpaceX additional acreage

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:41.960
for expanded launch infrastructure

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.740
and return for conservation easements elsewhere.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:47.760
Plaintiffs argue the exchange violates

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.620
National Environmental Policy Act review requirements.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:54.340
A preliminary injunction hearing is expected within weeks.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.840
The US Fish and Wildlife Service approved the exchange

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.500
after determining that the conservation parcels

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.440
provide equivalent habitat value.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:06.000
Environmental groups contend that the agency failed

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.060
to prepare a supplemental environmental impact statement

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.920
before finalizing the transfer.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.140
SpaceX has stated that the additional land

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:16.500
would support expanded ground support equipment

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.000
for starship operations.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.080
Observers on NASA space flight forums

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:25.060
are tracking the second land space Zouke III landing attempt

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.620
after the rocket's successful debut flight from Juquan.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.280
The Chinese methane rocket completed its first flight

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.400
earlier this year and is now preparing

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.600
for a propulsive landing demonstration at the same site.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.440
Forum members are comparing telemetry

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.600
from the debut flight with public statements

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:46.140
from land space on grid fin and leg deployment sequences.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:48.800
Analysts note that a successful landing

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:50.500
would mark the first reuse attempt

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.800
by a Chinese orbital class booster.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:57.180
The Juquan launch site has limited downrange tracking assets

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:00.740
which may constrain real-time data during the descent burn.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:04.900
Chinese state media have not yet released a firm target date

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:05.920
for the second flight.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:09.920
Unverified imagery circulating on X shows what appears

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.400
to be a new grid fin actuator design

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.300
on an early starship test article at Starbase.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.660
The images depict a revised mounting bracket

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:21.740
and motor housing compared with earlier booster fins.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:25.740
Observers suggest the change could improve response time

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.100
or reduce mass in the fin control system.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.220
No official confirmation has come from SpaceX

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:34.440
on whether the actuator will fly on an upcoming vehicle.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.020
The photos were taken during routine ground transport

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.640
between the production building and the launch mount.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.360
Engineers on the same thread are debating whether the redesign

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:48.280
addresses thermal loads observed during previous re-entries.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.840
Residents near Boca Chica posted drone footage

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.760
of recent static fire vibrations

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:57.500
that they claim reached previously unrecorded amplitudes.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:00.760
The clips show visible shaking of nearby structures

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:03.120
during a Raptor engine test sequence.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.540
Posters timestamped the footage

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:09.500
to a specific ship static fire campaign conducted last week.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.480
Local measurements cited in the post exceed amplitudes recorded

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:17.460
by SpaceX's own seismic monitors in prior public reports.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.240
The footage has been shared in community groups

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.260
monitoring Boca Chica test activity.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:25.820
No independent verification of the amplitude claims

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:28.300
has been published by third party seismologists.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.860
From an engineering standpoint,

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:34.380
Raptor 3's shift to a full-flow staged combustion cycle

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:36.740
routes every molecule of methane and oxygen

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.640
through the respective turbo pumps

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.580
before they reach the injector.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.900
This eliminates the separate gas generator stage

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:46.220
that previously dumped hot gas overboard,

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:49.620
raising overall efficiency while removing several valves

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:50.540
and manifolds.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:53.860
The resulting part count reduction directly attacks

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:57.400
the idiot index, or earlier Raptors carried an estimated

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:01.020
four to five times markup over raw materials in labor.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:04.320
And the new architecture targets closer to three times

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:05.980
by collapsing assembly steps.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:09.140
That lower index matters because each starship

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:10.300
needs dozens of engines.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.900
Even a 20% drop in engine cost multiplies

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:15.260
across the booster and ship.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.080
The design choice also buys margin on chamber pressure

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.960
without increasing turbo pump stress,

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.380
because the pre-burners now operate

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:25.940
at the same mixture ratio as the main chamber.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:28.880
Next, watch for the first integrated test

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:31.700
of a full Raptor 3 set on a ship or booster,

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:32.980
static fire stand.

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:36.460
If the simplified plumbing survives the thermal environment

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:40.060
at 280 TF, the program gains a credible path

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:42.900
to the production rate required for monthly flight attempts.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:48.260
In a quick market node, SPC X is at $160.95.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:51.980
Before we go, Starship's next engineering milestone

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:54.240
remains the first tower catch attempt

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:56.440
once Raptor 3 production stabilizes.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.860
That's your SpaceX news for today.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:03.200
SPC X closed at $160.95.

